WasmFS: poll() takes empty files and devices for unreadable

poll() reported POLLIN only for a file whose size was above zero, so an
empty regular file, /dev/null and /dev/random never polled readable. Give
data files a readiness hook that defaults to readable, and let pipes report
whether they hold data.

Upstream: not filed yet
Draft: docs/upstream/emscripten-wasmfs-poll-regular-file.md

diff --git a/system/lib/wasmfs/file.h b/system/lib/wasmfs/file.h
index 7e299cd..88d5f57 100644
--- a/system/lib/wasmfs/file.h
+++ b/system/lib/wasmfs/file.h
@@ -152,6 +152,10 @@ protected:
   // on success or a negative error code.
   virtual int flush() = 0;
 
+  // Whether poll() should report the file readable. Files whose readiness can
+  // change, like pipes, override this.
+  virtual bool isReadReady() { return true; }
+
 public:
   static constexpr FileKind expectedKind = File::DataFileKind;
   DataFile(mode_t mode, backend_t backend)
@@ -366,6 +370,8 @@ public:
 
   [[nodiscard]] int setSize(off_t size) { return getFile()->setSize(size); }
 
+  bool isReadReady() { return getFile()->isReadReady(); }
+
   // TODO: Design a proper API for flushing files.
   [[nodiscard]] int flush() { return getFile()->flush(); }
 
diff --git a/system/lib/wasmfs/pipe_backend.h b/system/lib/wasmfs/pipe_backend.h
